/bin/
coverage.*
# `go build ./...` drops one binary per main package into the repo ROOT, named
# after its directory. One of them, `claimlag`, was committed by accident: a
# 9.3 MB Mach-O carrying 117 embedded /Users paths and a client symbol that
# `strings` did not surface. Every main package is listed so the next one cannot
# repeat it. Regenerate with:
#   go list -f '{{if eq .Name "main"}}/{{.Dir}}{{end}}' ./... | sed 's|.*/|/|'
/appfocus
/attributionskip
/claimlag
/claimset
/confidential
/consolidatecheck
