# Claude Code agent worktrees (transient, machine-local)
.claude/worktrees/

# Findings that are about the client surface rather than about the tool. The
# rest of project/ is deliberately published: it is the measurement trail
# CLAUDE.md calls load-bearing, and it survives here intact. What does not
# belong in a public tree is a document whose subject IS what was removed --
# such a document is a map of the surface, and publishing the map undoes the
# pass. This is a directory rather than a list of filenames on purpose: an
# ignore entry naming a dated confidentiality document is itself a pointer to
# one. Contents stay on disk and in the private mirror's history.
/project/private/

# Design mockups and other binary working material. These are large -- 25 MB at
# the time this entry was added -- and they are not the measurement trail that
# the rest of project/ exists to publish. A document that needs an image should
# say in words what the image shows, so that the published record still stands
# on its own for a reader who never had the file.
/project/images/
